<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zungeru</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zungeru is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> State, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a> made it the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-nigeria-protectorate">Protectorate of Northern Nigeria</a> in 1902, replacing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lokoja">Lokoja</a>, and it remained the seat of government until the move to Kaduna in 1917. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nnamdi-azikiwe">Nnamdi Azikiwe</a>, Nigeria's first president, was born there in 1904.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zungeru.jpg" alt="Zungeru" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeremy Weate from Abuja, Nigeria · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nnamdi_Azikiwe%27s_birthplace,_Zungeru.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
